(2)	Physical assessments evaluate assets for evidence of unauthorized access and/or modifications.', 'Approved procedure or standard for logical tampering protection defining scope, accountable roles and required asset records; sample asset records or system exports demonstrating the control is implemented for critical assets; periodic review, inspection or exception-tracking evidence showing the control remains accurate and maintained.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-016', 'OT', 'Asset Management', 'Technology Asset Inspections', 'Mechanisms exist to physically and logically inspect critical technology assets to detect evidence of tampering.', 'Approved procedure or standard for technology asset inspections defining scope, accountable roles and required asset records; sample asset records or system exports demonstrating the control is implemented for critical assets; periodic review, inspection or exception-tracking evidence showing the control remains accurate and maintained.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-017', 'OT', 'Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery', 'Data Backups', 'Mechanisms exist to create recurring backups of data, software and/or system images, as well as verify the integrity of these backups, to ensure the availability of the data to satisfy Recovery Time Objectives (RTOs) and Recovery Point Objectives (RPOs).', 'Backup policy and schedule defining systems, frequency, retention, ownership and backup protection requirements; backup job success/failure logs for critical systems; restore test records proving data can be recovered within agreed recovery objectives.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-018', 'OT', 'Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery', 'Separate Storage for Critical Information', 'Mechanisms exist to store backup copies of critical software and other security-related information in a separate facility or in a fire-rated container that is not collocated with the system being backed up.', 'Backup policy and schedule defining systems, frequency, retention, ownership and backup protection requirements; backup job success/failure logs for critical systems; restore test records proving data can be recovered within agreed recovery objectives.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-019', 'OT', 'Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery', 'Test Restoration Using Sampling', 'Mechanisms exist to utilize sampling of available backups to test recovery capabilities as part of business continuity plan testing.', 'Backup policy and schedule defining systems, frequency, retention, ownership and backup protection requirements; backup job success/failure logs for critical systems; restore test records proving data can be recovered within agreed recovery objectives.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-020', 'OT', 'Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery', 'Technology Assets, Applications and/or Services (TAAS) Recovery & Reconstitution', 'Mechanisms exist to ensure the secure recovery and reconstitution of Technology Assets, Applications and/or Services (TAAS) to a known state after a disruption, compromise or failure.', 'Approved recovery runbooks describing how critical services are restored, validated and returned to normal operations; recovery priority list aligned to business impact analysis; exercise or incident records showing essential functions were resumed using defined criteria and approvals.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-021', 'OT', 'Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery', 'Business Continuity Management System (BCMS)', 'Mechanisms exist to facilitate the implementation of contingency planning controls to help ensure resilient Technology Assets, Applications and/or Services (TAAS) (e.g., Continuity of Operations Plan (COOP) or Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery (BC/DR) playbooks).', 'Approved BCMS framework or policy defining continuity governance, roles, scope and maintenance requirements; business impact analysis and continuity strategy for critical operations; BC/DR exercise reports and management review records showing plans are tested, updated and approved.', 'seed_script'),
        ('CII-CID-022', 'OT', 'Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery', 'Recovery Operations Criteria', 'Mechanisms exist to define specific criteria that must be met to initiate Business Continuity / Disaster Recover (BC/DR) plans that facilitate business continuity operations capable of meeting applicable Recovery Time Objectives (RTOs) and Recovery Point Objectives (RPOs).', 'Business impact analysis documenting approved RTO and RPO for critical business and operational services; recovery strategy mapping systems to required recovery objectives; test results or exercise reports demonstrating whether actual recovery performance meets the approved targets.', 'seed_script'),
